.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="In 1807 Humphry Davy passed current through molten potash and soda and isolated potassium and sodium -- metals no chemical reducing agent of the day could free, because their reduction potentials are among the most negative in the electrochemical series. This example ranks Davy&#x27;s two couples against the rest of STANDARD_REDUCTION_POTENTIALS, shows why the common reducing metals (Zn, Fe) cannot reduce K+ or Na+, computes the minimum electrolysis voltage for the molten chlorides with minimum_applied_voltage_electrolytic, and uses Faraday&#x27;s law to estimate how much potassium a current yields.">

